{"nodes": [{"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing", "label": "Implementing Sleek Designs in React Native / Expo", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_version_selection", "label": "Which Version to Use", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "activeVersion is nullable, so default to the versions entry whose version equals activeVersion and fall back to the highest numeric version; the selected entry's id must also be passed in componentVersionOverrides because the renderer can otherwise produce an empty frame. If there are no versions at all, stop and report that there is no code to implement."}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_pinned_versions", "label": "Pinned Component and Theme Versions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_design_tokens", "label": "Design Token Porting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The project theme is inlined into every screen, so it is ported once into a single token module that every component reads from. --radius is a base that must be resolved with calc() into concrete numbers, --shape must be tested by value rather than presence because React Native has no corner-shape, and unsupported colour formats are converted once while supported ones are preserved."}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_icons", "label": "Iconify Icon Porting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use the exact icon set and name found in the HTML because matching icons carry design fidelity. On Expo the mdi:* prefix is a free rename to MaterialCommunityIcons; other prefixes go through the Iconify SVG API and are rendered with react-native-svg's SvgXml so no extra native dependency is needed."}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_fonts", "label": "Font Porting from Theme Families", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The head link tags give font families, not the weights used; the real weights live in the body's font-* Tailwind classes, so only those faces are bundled. An exported alias like --font-font-heading does not define the font-heading utility, so malformed aliases are corrected when porting and any remaining discrepancy with the screenshot is recorded rather than silently resolved."}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_flex_direction", "label": "Flex Direction Row/Column Trap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sleek writes the web idiom where display:flex is a row, but React Native defaults flexDirection to column, so a horizontal row silently renders as a vertical stack. Every flex in the source must be given an explicit direction; flex-1 maps to flex:1 and inline-flex is dropped with a value warning."}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_text_wrapping", "label": "Strings Must Live Inside <Text>", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every string must be rendered inside <Text>, including strings hidden in && branches, ternaries or stray {' '}. A bare string under a <View> fails silently: the New Architecture routes the warning through console.error, so in a production build the string simply disappears and nothing throws."}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_safe_area_insets", "label": "Safe Area Insets", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The mockup renders edge to edge with no notch, status bar or home indicator, so an unguarded screen draws under the system bars; Expo SDK 54+ makes Android edge-to-edge the default. Insets come from react-native-safe-area-context rather than React Native's own SafeAreaView, which only insets on iOS, and each edge is inset exactly once."}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_shadows", "label": "Cross-Platform Shadows", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "boxShadow maps the mockup's CSS shadow 1:1 on both platforms and is the default choice because React Native only ships the New Architecture from 0.82. Legacy projects must set iOS shadowColor/shadowOffset/shadowOpacity/shadowRadius plus Android elevation and a backgroundColor, accepting that Android only approximates the exact shadow."}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_route_tree", "label": "Infer the Route Tree from the Screen Set", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each Sleek screen is a standalone document that redraws the whole chrome, so the screen set must be read as one app and the navigator inferred before implementing: a repeated bottom bar means tab siblings, a back arrow means a Stack child, a hamburger means a Drawer, and horizontal tabs or a FAB are components rather than routes. The navigator owns the chrome and draws it once."}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_build_the_feature", "label": "Build the Feature, Not the Mockup", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A mockup shipped verbatim is a convincing dead app: structure, layout and styling are the spec, but names, numbers and copy are placeholders that must be replaced by real state, props or API data. A mockup also shows only one moment, so empty, single-item, loading and error states must be decided separately."}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_keyboard_avoidance", "label": "Keyboard Avoidance for TextInput Screens", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_definition_of_done", "label": "Native Implementation Definition of Done", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing", "target": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_endpoints", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing", "target": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_version_selection", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing", "target": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_pinned_versions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing", "target": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_design_tokens", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing", "target": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_icons", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing", "target": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_fonts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/design-mobile-apps/implementing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing", "target": "agents_skills_design_mobile_apps_implementing_flex_direction", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_sc